    "result_text": "All 262 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS** (the stray stack-trace line is from a negative test `createUserNoRolesFails`, which reports 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. Every change centers on mixing a fixed `V2` tag into the *identifiers* only, while keeping the user-facing region fields plain.\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 algorithm):**\n- `src/main/java/.../util/OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 added a shared `VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` constant. `identityKey` now hashes `V2|<tel>|<email>|<soundex>` and a new `regionCode(region)` helper prepends the tag (e.g. `NSW` \u2192 `V2NSW`).\n- `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 `nextMemberId` now uses `OwnerIdentity.regionCode(region)` for the memberId's REGION segment (yielding e.g. `V2NSW2616E6609E9`, with the Luhn check recomputed), and `householdId` mixes the tag into its digest.\n\nBecause `V2` prepends the region and is folded into the household/identity hashes, every identifier differs from its v1 form and no v1 value can recur.\n\n**Region stays plain (never tagged):**\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 `formatLocality` no longer reads the memberId's (now v2-tagged) region segment; it resolves the plain region directly from postcode \u2192 city, so `locality` stays `NSW`, `timezone` stays correct, and `ownerSegment`'s METRO/REGIONAL derivation is recomputed from the plain region. Removed the now-unused `memberIdRegion` helper.\n\n**Response shape:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`, added a nested `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema) grouping those three, and a top-level integer `apiVersion` (2).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 new `formatIdentity(owner)` builds the nested `OwnerIdentityDto`; `apiVersion` mapped to `2`.\n\n**Audit schema v2:**\n- `audit/OwnerCreatedEvent.java` \u2014 added `SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`, emitted as `schemaVersion` in the JSON; the event carries the v2 memberId (the owner segment/identity is thereby recomputed from the v2 identity).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.",
