    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:651`). I've split it into what runs before the method body (framework layer) and what runs inside it, in execution order.\n\n## A. Before the method runs (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation** on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (constraints from the generated DTO), any failure \u2192 400:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` non-blank, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `title`: `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address`: `@Pattern` non-blank, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`\n\n## B. Inside `addOwner`, in order\n\n**Idempotency short-circuit (runs first)**\n3. Read the `Idempotency-Key` header. If it was seen before **and** the previously created owner still exists, recompute its derived fields and return it with **200 OK** \u2014 no new owner is created. (Blank/missing key is ignored.)\n\n**Validations (each throws and aborts on failure)**\n4. **Telephone** normalized to E.164 via `toE164`; if it can't form a valid E.164 number \u2192 **400**. (This also enforces the national-length rule for explicit `+61`/`+1` country codes.)\n5. **Email syntax** \u2014 if email is non-null and fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Disposable email domain** \u2014 if the email domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Address presence** \u2014 compose the address (structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` preferred, else flat `address`), normalized; if the result is empty \u2192 **400** (\"An address is required\").\n8. **Postcode** \u2014 if postcode is non-null and `isPostcodeValid` fails (not 4 digits, or out of the city's region range) \u2192 **400**.\n9. **Registration date not in future** \u2014 if supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Daily registration limit** \u2014 count owners already on the business-day-adjusted registration date; if `>= 100` \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n11. **City capacity** \u2014 count owners in the (normalized) city; if `>= 50` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n12. **Identity-duplicate check** \u2014 build the identity key (E.164 telephone + lower-cased email + Soundex of last name); if any non-deleted owner shares it \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n\n**Non-fatal derivations computed before save**\n13. Compute the effective/business-day registration date (defaults to today if omitted, rolled forward off weekends/public holidays).\n14. Compute `householdId` (when postcode present).\n15. Compute `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 a soft match: an existing non-deleted owner with same postcode and last-name Soundex but a different identity key.\n16. Compute `namesakeCount` \u2014 existing owners with the same normalized first+last name.\n\n**Side-effects (mutations / persistence / outbound), in order**\n17. Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` and set: `namesakeCount`, composed `address`, `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (nulled when flat form used), E.164 `telephone`, lower-cased `email`, business-day `registrationDate`, a **deduplicated `memberId`** (`nextMemberId` + `deduplicateMemberId`), `householdId`, `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n18. **Persist** the owner \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (assigns the id).\n19. If an idempotency key was present, **record** `idempotencyKey \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory `idempotentCreations` map.\n20. Set `householdSize` and compute the capped `membershipLevel`.\n21. **Audit log** (`AUDIT` logger): human-readable \"owner created: id/memberId/registrationDate/membershipLevel\" line.\n22. **Structured audit event** (`AUDIT` logger): immutable `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON stamped with a **monotonic sequence number** (`CREATE_SEQUENCE.incrementAndGet()`).\n23. **Welcome notification** (`NOTIFY` logger): \"welcome notification: ownerId/memberId\".\n24. Build the response `OwnerDto` and set the transient flags `membershipLevel`, `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 owners that day), `capacityWarning` (city at 40\u201349), `riskFlag`; set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`; return **201 CREATED**.\n\nA couple of notes worth flagging: the `sharesHousehold` field in the DTO is not consulted anywhere in `addOwner` (household membership is now governed purely by the derived `householdId`/ceiling), and the entire validation/count/duplicate path uses `findAllOwners()` scans with no locking, so the daily-limit, city-capacity, and identity-uniqueness checks are not concurrency-safe against simultaneous creates."
